name: fraud_premium_rate
title: "Premium-rate runbook"
summary: "Detects: charge to the ranges in `premium_prefixes` (E.164, so `999900` is national `0900`), per caller, above `threshold` (default 100)."
steps[4]:
  - text: "Detects: charge to the ranges in `premium_prefixes` (E.164, so `999900` is national `0900`), per caller, above `threshold` (default 100)."
    link:
      kind: dataset
      id: fraud_premium_rate
  - text: "Check: is the premium-rate number owned by a known content partner? Is the traffic machine-regular?"
  - text: "Act: bar premium-rate access on the line; hold the partner's revenue share."
  - text: "Silent by design: an occasional premium-rate user."
ownerRole: fraud-analyst
tags[2]: fraud, telco
